% bring_and_push - bring it to the edge of a drop, then force it in
%
% The need is an enemy with status ?s. This way of meeting it: ground whose
% hazard does ?s to whatever enters it (the void: fallen), and a region at
% its edge the enemy can be brought to. Bring the enemy to the edge, then
% force it in. Who brings it is decided by who holds a pull, a push or a dash
% (bringTo); who forces it in, by who holds a forced movement that moves it.
%
% The drop is never walked into: the only link into it runs one way, from
% the edge, and it is not a region anyone stands in to cast from.

bringAndPush(?e, ?s) :-
    if(role(?e, enemy), not(status(?e, ?s)),
       hazard(?feat, ?s), regionHas(?drop, ?feat), connected(?edge, ?drop), region(?edge)),
    do(bringTo(?e, ?edge), forceInto(?e, ?drop)).

% Forced movement: whatever moves ?e without its consent - a push away from
% the caster or a pull toward it, unless ?e is immune to it. Nothing is pulled
% into a drop (nobody stands beyond it). A taunt is not one: the taunter goes
% along.
forceInto(?e, ?to) :- if(), do(push(?e, ?to)).
forceInto(?e, ?to) :- if(), do(lure(?e, ?to)).
